From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:12:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] eal/windows: do not install sched.h with MinGW

Since commit ad645a9317 ("eal/windows: install sched.h file"), meson
install copies lib/eal/windows/include/sched.h into the include
directory of the prefix. The C library of MSVC has no sched.h, so that
is right for MSVC and clang. MinGW has a sched.h of its own, in
winpthreads, and an install of DPDK into the MinGW prefix (for example
/mingw64 of MSYS2) replaces it. Each later user of pthread.h of that
toolchain then stops:

  /mingw64/include/sched.h:29:35: error: 'RTE_MAX_LCORE' undeclared
  /mingw64/include/pthread.h:218:24: error: field 'param' has
  incomplete type

Install the file only when the compiler is not GCC. A MinGW build of an
application takes the DPDK sched.h from the DPDK source tree, as it did
before v24.07.

Fixes: ad645a9317 ("eal/windows: install sched.h file")

Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 lib/eal/windows/include/meson.build | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/eal/windows/include/meson.build b/lib/eal/windows/include/meson.build
index e985a77d58..a8ffdd5a3d 100644
--- a/lib/eal/windows/include/meson.build
+++ b/lib/eal/windows/include/meson.build
@@ -6,5 +6,13 @@ includes += include_directories('.')
 headers += files(
         'rte_os.h',
         'rte_windows.h',
-        'sched.h',
 )
+
+# The C library of MSVC has no sched.h, so DPDK installs its own. MinGW has
+# one (winpthreads), and an install into the MinGW prefix replaces it: each
+# pthread.h user of that toolchain then stops with "'RTE_MAX_LCORE'
+# undeclared". A MinGW build of an application takes the DPDK sched.h from
+# the DPDK source tree, as before v24.07.
+if cc.get_id() != 'gcc'
+    headers += files('sched.h')
+endif
